[[DeFoe]] had his Suits pursue [[Lok Lambert]] in an attempt to retrieve [[Eathon Lambert's journal]] and its secrets of the [[Amulet of Will]]. {{source|A Seeker Is Born}} Pursuing the Foundation's clue regarding the [[Metagolem|Golem]], [[the Organization]] gained [[Jodis Lore's Key]]. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}} The team was later sent to [[Rouen, France]], to retrieve [[Gar-Ghoul]]. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}}

However, they missed the more important information on the [[Ring of Arc]] and were then sent by [[the Professor]] to [[Paris, France]], following Dante's team into the [[Paris Catacombs]]. {{source|Crawling the Catacombs}} Despite gaining a number of new recruits from Paris, they were unsuccessful at retrieving the Ring. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}

His Suits were later sent after [[King Basilisk]], but lost the Titan to [[Zhalia Moon]]. They also lost [[unnamed Suit 001]] to a petrification trap within the Titan's chamber. {{source|Absent Heroes}}

Upon this failure, DeFoe lost command of his original team of Suits and thus had to rally his remaining loyal Suits within [[Velo, Greece]], in an attempt to finally get his revenge on [[Dante Vale]]. This team failed and were escorted back under [[Grier]]. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

DeFoe's former Suits were placed under [[Rassimov]] and given an improved arsenal of Titans. They were then sent by Rassimov to ambush [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]], who were working at a burger joint in [[Venice, Italy]]. The Suits were defeated by Lok and Sophie, who were joined by [[Zhalia Moon]]. {{source|All Work and No Pay}}

Two of the recruits from Paris, also formerly under DeFoe, were sent by Rassimov in an attempt to eliminate [[Sophie Casterwill]] and company. They failed to hinder the Foundation members, however. More of his Suits, who had infiltrated the [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot]], confronted the Foundation team but were swiftly defeated. {{source|Memory Lane}}

His own team of Suits were then sent by [[the Professor]] to the coasts of [[Turkey]] in search for the [[Ring]] of [[Behemoth]]. Though two of his Suits were overpowering the native [[Amazons]], they were defeated by Dante, Lok, and Sophie. Rassimov later joined his team, but the Suits were defeated Dante received the Ring of Behemoth from [[Zhalia Moon]]. {{source|Ladies' Choice}}

Rassimov and his suits travelled to the [[Temple of Poseidon]] to beat Dante's team to the [[Amulet of Will]] but were unable to stop them from getting through the entrance to [[Atlantis]]. {{source|The Unseen Guide}} Upon eventually catching up with the Huntik team at the Casterwill compound, they fought against Zhalia and Sophie while Lok and Rassimov battled one-on-one. They were defeated however, with numerous Suits being turned to stone by King Basilisk. {{source|Coming of Age}}

Rassimov and his team along with the Professor and his two elite agents travelled to [[King Solomon's Mines]] on the trail of the Ring of [[Tao]]. They pursued the Huntik team and their guide [[Otto]] via car but were stopped when Metagolem demolished the [[Ndago bridge]]. They later attacked the team in the desert before taking Zhalia and Otto prisoner. {{source|The Golden Asp}} After entering the Mines, two of Rassimov's suits were deployed to stop the team but failed. Later the Suits fought aginst the Huntik team and [[Montehue]] and [[Tersly]]. Despite overpowering the Foundation's forces, they were forced to retreat when Lok bonded with Tao. {{source|To Be Together}}

A number of Rassimov's Suits were positioned at [[The Professor's castle]] but were defeated by the Dante's team. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

The Professor and his two elite agents travelled to [[King Solomon's Mines]] on the trail of the Ring of [[Tao]]. {{source|The Golden Asp}} After entering the Mines, the Suits fought aginst the Huntik team and [[Montehue]] and [[Tersly]]. Despite overpowering the Foundation's forces, they were forced to retreat when Lok bonded with Tao. {{source|To Be Together}}

The two agents later attacked Dante's house and left the team considerably injured and worse for wear. {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}} They fought against the team at the Professor's castle but were defeated. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

Following the Professor's defeat, the two agents attacked the Huntik team after they broke into Organisation central but were defeated. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Under the command of [[Wilder]] and [[Hoffman]], the two agents defended the Professor's castle from Dante and Grier before being defeated. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

